  "description": "Maryland's 5th Congressional District will elect a new representative in 2026 after 20-term incumbent Steny Hoyer (D) announced his retirement. The district spans Southern Maryland including Calvert, Charles, and St. Mary's counties plus portions of Prince George's and Anne Arundel counties. With Democrats outnumbering Republicans more than 2-to-1, the June 23 Democratic primary is widely viewed as the decisive contest. More than 20 Democrats filed, led by Hoyer-endorsed Delegate Adrian Boafo, former Capitol Police officer Harry Dunn, healthcare CEO Quincy Bareebe, and former Prince George's County Executive Rushern Baker III. Three Republicans are also competing in their primary.",
